.\" Manual page for the polycall command-line tool.
.\" Keep in sync with the command registry in src/cli/cli_commands.c and
.\" with docs/CLI.md (the authoritative CLI contract).
.TH POLYCALL 1 2026-10-12 PolyCall "User Commands"
.SH NAME
polycall \- program\-first cross\-language runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B polycall
.RI [ global\-options ]
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B polycall
is the command\-line interface to the PolyCall runtime.
A caller sends a service name, an operation name and a JSON input over the
.B polycall_rpc
v1 wire protocol; the runtime routes the request to whichever process
registered that
.I service.operation
and returns a typed JSON result or a structured error, regardless of the
language the operation is implemented in.
.PP
Run with no arguments,
.B polycall
prints help and exits 0.
Non\-interactive input never starts an interactive session;
.B polycall repl
is the only way into one.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR help " [\fIcommand\fR [\fIsubcommand\fR]]"
Show help for polycall or for a specific command.
.TP
.B version
Print the version as a single line and exit.
.TP
.B doctor
Report build, platform, ABI and core\-capability status.
This is read\-only: it never starts a service, opens a socket or evaluates a
configuration provider.
.TP
.BR "config validate" " [\fB\-\-provider\fR \fBc:\fILIB\fR|\fBnode:\fIMOD\fR|\fBpython:\fIMOD\fR | \fB\-\-envelope\fR \fIFILE\fR | \fIpath\fR]"
Validate a native configuration provider or canonical envelope through the
typed configuration model, or, with no selector, a legacy
.I Polycallfile
through the legacy loader.
.TP
.BR "config show" " [\fIselector\fR | \fIlanguage\fR] [\fB\-\-provenance\fR]"
Print the effective configuration, optionally with the winning source of
each field.
.TP
.BR "config load" " [\fIlanguage\fR]"
Load the legacy configuration hierarchy and report the order.
.TP
.BR "config migrate" " \fIsrc\fR \fBPolycallrc.\fIlang\fR | \fB\-\-from\-legacy\fR [\fB\-\-language\fR \fIL\fR] \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR"
Copy\-migrate a legacy file to its language\-native name, or convert the
legacy effective model into a schema\-v2 envelope.
Never overwrites an existing file.
.TP
.BR "telemetry emit" " \fB\-\-event\fR \fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-service\fR \fIS\fR] [\fB\-\-operation\fR \fIOP\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR \fIST\fR] [\fB\-\-detail\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-correlation\-id\fR \fIGUID\fR]"
Append one GUID and timestamp correlated event to the telemetry sink and
print the correlation id used.
.TP
.BR "telemetry show" " [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]"
Print the most recent recorded events (default 20, newest last).
.TP
.B telemetry status
Report whether telemetry is enabled and where it writes.
.TP
.B repl
Start an explicit interactive session over the same command set.
.TP
.BR start " [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIhost\fB:\fIport\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR] [\fB\-\-endpoint\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-load\fR \fIPATH\fR ...] [\fB\-\-daemon\fR]"
Start the runtime in the foreground and serve the built\-in operations
.RB ( inventory.get ", " debug.sleep )
plus any operations added by
.B \-\-load
plugins, until interrupted or stopped with an authenticated
.BR "polycall stop" .
The default endpoint is
.BR 127.0.0.1:0 ;
port 0 binds an ephemeral port, which is written to
.B \-\-endpoint\-file
when given.
.B \-\-load
loads one operation plugin (a shared library exporting
.BR polycall_ops_register );
an ABI mismatch or missing symbol fails before anything is bound.
.B \-\-daemon
detaches into the background and prints the detached process ID.
.TP
.BR status " \fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIhost\fB:\fIport\fR"
Describe the registered operations of a running instance over its control
channel.
.TP
.BR stop " \fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIhost\fB:\fIport\fR [\fB\-\-auth\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]"
Ask a running instance to shut down.
.TP
.BR call " \fISERVICE OPERATION\fR \fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIhost\fB:\fIport\fR [\fB\-\-input\fR \fIFILE\fR|\fB\-\fR | \fB\-\-input\-value\fR \fIJSON\fR] [\fB\-\-deadline\-ms\fR \fIN\fR]"
Invoke a registered operation with exactly one round trip and no retry.
The deadline defaults to
.B \-\-timeout\-ms
when given, otherwise 5000 ms.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options are accepted before or after the command words, but never
after
.BR \-\- .
Both
.BI \-\-opt= value
and
.BI \-\-opt " value"
forms are accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-project\-root " PATH"
Project root that relative paths, and the default telemetry sink, resolve
against.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Explicit configuration file or provider.
.TP
.BI \-\-language " LANG"
Language layer or adapter to select.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " \fBtext\fR|\fBjson\fR"
Output format for finite commands (default
.BR text ).
With
.BR json ,
exactly one JSON object is printed on standard output for success and
failure alike.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-essential text on standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout\-ms " N"
Deadline for operations that support one.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option parsing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime or internal failure.
.TP
.B 2
Command\-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Invalid or missing selected configuration (also: malformed operation input).
.TP
.B 4
Missing dependency, adapter, unsupported capability, or unknown operation
or item.
.TP
.B 5
Transport failure or endpoint unavailable.
.TP
.B 6
Operation deadline exceeded.
.TP
.B 7
Authentication or authorization rejected.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by the user (SIGINT).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POLYCALL_TELEMETRY
Set to
.BR off ", " 0 ", " false " or " no
to disable telemetry entirely.
.TP
.B POLYCALL_TELEMETRY_LOG
Path of the telemetry sink, overriding the default.
.TP
.BR POLYCALL_NODE_PROVIDER ", " POLYCALL_PYTHON_PROVIDER
Runner script used to evaluate a
.BR node: " or " python:
configuration provider.
.TP
.B POLYCALL_PYTHON
Python interpreter used for
.B python:
providers (default
.BR python3 ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Polycallfile
Writable project topology (legacy format).
.TP
.IR Polycallrc ", " Polycallrc. language
Read\-only runtime defaults and per\-language overrides (legacy format).
.TP
.IB project\-root /.polycall/telemetry.jsonl
Default telemetry sink: one JSON event per line.
The project root defaults to the current directory.
.SH NOTES
The native configuration schema accepts TLS settings, but no TLS library is
linked: the runtime speaks plaintext
.B polycall_rpc
v1 and binds the loopback interface by default.
Use
.B \-\-auth\-token
when other local users must not be able to stop the runtime.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a runtime on an ephemeral port, call the built\-in operation, and stop
it again:
.PP
.nf
.RS
polycall start \-\-endpoint 127.0.0.1:0 \-\-endpoint\-file /tmp/ep \e
    \-\-auth\-token secret \-\-daemon
polycall call inventory get \-\-endpoint "$(cat /tmp/ep)" \e
    \-\-input\-value \(aq{"item_id":"widget\-a"}\(aq
polycall stop \-\-endpoint "$(cat /tmp/ep)" \-\-auth\-token secret
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The CLI contract, wire protocol and plugin ABI are documented at
.UR https://github.com/obinexus/polycall
.UE
(docs/CLI.md, docs/RPC.md and docs/PLUGINS.md).
